      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Flowable's job is sequencing: it decides *when* a step runs and who it is waiting on. The artefact it leaves behind is a mutable process or case instance row, and its history is purgeable. That means the engine that knew the decision was taken is also the engine that can be made to forget it, which is a different guarantee from the one an auditor asks for.\n\nThe seam follows directly. Powerhouse holds the append-only, user-attributed record of what was decided, and Flowable calls a Switchboard mutation at each decision point. Nothing is taken away from the orchestrator: it keeps control flow, task assignment and timers. What moves out is the durable answer to \"who approved this, under which rule, and what was the state before\". The research text notes this is the same gap as Camunda and the same seam \u2014 the finding is about the category of BPMN engines, not about one vendor's implementation.\n\nCommercially the useful detail is the installed base. Flowable's partner base is heavily banking and insurance, where \"who approved this, under which rule\" is already a funded question rather than one that has to be created. The buyer does not need convincing that attribution matters; the conversation starts at whether the existing engine answers it. Across the 35 partners carrying this finding \u2014 mostly CH, DE and US \u2014 that shortens the pitch to a demonstration rather than an argument.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (35)\n\n**2 \u00b7 next**\n- Creetion (NL Breda) \u2014 creetion.com\n- Masoona Consulting GmbH (DE Nuremberg) \u2014 masoona.de\n- XTi NV (BE Kontich/Hasselt/Merelbeke) \u2014 xt-i.com\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Counterpoint Consulting (US Reston VA) \u2014 counterpointconsulting.com\n- Digital Workforce (FI Helsinki) \u2014 digitalworkforce.com\n- ELCA Group (CH Pully/Lausanne + 4 cities) \u2014 elca.ch\n- Eraneos (CH Zurich) \u2014 eraneos.com\n- Fincons Group (IT Milan + CH/DE/FR/UK/US) \u2014 finconsgroup.com\n- Forty2 AG (CH Cham/Zug + DE/LU/PT/ES) \u2014 forty2.ch\n- GFT Technologies SE (DE Stuttgart + IT/PL delivery) \u2014 gft.com\n- Groupe Onepoint (FR Paris + 7 cities) \u2014 groupeonepoint.com\n- LionGate AG (DE Munich) \u2014 liongate.de\n- Mesoneer AG (CH Zurich) \u2014 mesoneer.io\n- Nortal (EE Tallinn) \u2014 nortal.com\n- Pragmatica AG (CH + EU/SG/HK) \u2014 pragmatica.ch\n- Synpulse (CH Zurich) \u2014 synpulse.com\n- adesso Group (CH Zurich + DE + AT) \u2014 adesso.ch\n- it-novum GmbH (DE Fulda) \u2014 eim.it-novum.com\n- ti&m AG (CH Zurich + Bern/Basel/Frankfurt/Duesseldorf) \u2014 ti8m.com\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Accenture (IE Dublin / global) \u2014 accenture.com\n- BehaimITS (US Chicago IL) \u2014 behaimits.com\n- Clarium (US Miami FL) \u2014 clarium.tech\n- EPAM Systems (US Newtown PA / global) \u2014 epam.com\n- ERRY (CN Shanghai) \u2014 erry.com\n- Fulcrum Digital (US Jersey City NJ) \u2014 fulcrumdigital.com\n- Kurulum (TR Istanbul) \u2014 kurul.com.tr\n- Merkle (dentsu) (US Columbia MD) \u2014 merkle.com\n- Myridius (US Princeton NJ) \u2014 myridius.com\n- Perficient (US St. Louis MO) \u2014 perficient.com\n- STP house (IL Netanya) \u2014 stphouse.com\n- Tata Consultancy Services (IN Mumbai / global) \u2014 tcs.com\n- dxdy (US + LK/SG) \u2014 dxdydigital.com\n\n**unprioritised**\n- Avaloq (CH Zurich) \u2014 avaloq.com\n- Exentra GmbH (DE) \u2014 exentra.de\n- eligamo AG (CH) \u2014 eligamo.com\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Flowable orchestrates WHEN things happen \u2014 the process/case instance is a mutable row and history is purgeable. Same gap as Camunda, same seam: Powerhouse holds the append-only, user-attributed record of what was decided, and Flowable calls a Switchboard mutation at each decision point. Flowable's base is heavily banking/insurance, where 'who approved this, under which rule' is already a funded question.\n\n## Scope: this holds for the Apache-2.0 edition\nPrimary-source research bounded this claim after it was written, and the bound matters commercially.\n\n**Where it still holds.** The OSS engine's own MyBatis mapper issues `update ${prefix}ACT_HI_PROCINST` with `START_TIME_` assignable, so mutability is quotable from source rather than inferred \u2014 see [[Flowable's engine issues UPDATE against its own history table]].\n\n**Where it does not.** Flowable **Enterprise** shipped a business audit trail on **2025-12-16** whose records are documented as immutable, procurable on-premise from a Swiss vendor with a Berlin office under ISO 27001 \u2014 so no sovereignty exclusion remains either. See [[Flowable shipped an immutable business audit trail in December 2025]].\n\n**And \"purgeable\" overstates the default.** Automatic history cleanup is **disabled by default** and retention is effectively infinite until an operator turns it on \u2014 see [[Flowable's automatic history cleanup is disabled by default]].\n\nThe seam described above is unchanged for an Apache-2.0 deployment. What changes is the sales argument: against a Flowable Enterprise incumbent it is a price-and-features comparison, not \"Flowable cannot do this\".\n",
